{"chunk_id": "f880dcabb083", "text": "This section continues the story of Drona\u2019s rise as the martial teacher of the Kuru princes. After being insulted and rejected by King Drupada, Drona arrives in Hastinapura and is honored by Bhishma, who entrusts all the Kuru princes\u2014both Pandavas and Kauravas\u2014to his instruction. Arjuna quickly distinguishes himself through intense discipline, cleverness, and devotion to his teacher, winning Drona\u2019s special favor. The episode of Ekalavya reveals a darker side of the social order: though denied formal training because of his birth, Ekalavya teaches himself by worshipping a clay image of Drona and becomes a master archer, only to sacrifice his thumb as \"tuition\" when Drona demands it to preserve Arjuna\u2019s supremacy. The chapter also establishes the specialties of each prince and ends with Drona preparing a famous test of skill\u2014the bird\u2019s-eye archery challenge.\nDrona trains the Kuru princes; Arjuna proves most devoted, Ekalavya sacrifices his thumb, and rivalries among the students intensify.\nThemes: teacher\u2013student devotion, jealousy and rivalry, social hierarchy and exclusion, sacrifice for guru, rise of Arjuna", "vector": [0.0023383593652397394, -0.026976721361279488, -0.016805607825517654, -0.0012431362411007285, -0.007119780406355858, 0.027442067861557007, -0.0181218683719635, -0.003623044351115823, -0.024822838604450226, -0.0249159075319767, -0.0035432707518339157, -0.00011083108256570995, 0.020621437579393387, 0.004354300908744335, -0.0006568845128640532, -0.00675747636705637, 0.040604688227176666, -0.02000983990728855, 0.006358609069138765, -0.026405012235045433, -0.0118928924202919, -0.009625996463000774, -0.003898927476257086, 0.009233777411282063, -0.014518768526613712, 0.03031391091644764, 0.007013415917754173, -0.030180955305695534, 0.002836943371221423, -0.010636460036039352, -0.003676226595416665, 0.004354300908744335, 0.0024746388662606478, -0.010097989812493324, -0.0346748